WEBVTT

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.480
The system is designed so you

00:00:01.359 --> 00:00:03.040
can generate a significant portion

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:04.780
of your ontology directly from an

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:06.520
existing power BI semantic model.

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:08.500
That makes total sense because a

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:10.340
semantic model already is a form

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:11.080
of an ontology.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.080
It has the tables, the relationships,

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:14.179
the business logic.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:16.660
How seamless is that translation process?

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:19.320
The ontology agent essentially ingests

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.820
the structure you've already built.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.800
The tables, columns, and established

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:24.800
relationships in your Power BI model

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:26.680
automatically provide the scaffolding

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:28.420
for the ontologies, entities, and properties.
